WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.441
Greetings and Introducing Yourself.

2
00:00:02.721 --> 00:00:06.134
Day 1 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

3
00:00:07.884 --> 00:00:08.908
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.188 --> 00:00:17.167
Today's goal: greet anyone politely, introduce yourself in 30 seconds, and ask the first questions that start a conversation.

5
00:00:18.517 --> 00:00:19.370
Part 1.

6
00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.293
Greetings: which one to use.

7
00:00:22.543 --> 00:00:23.887
Here is a quick table:

8
00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:26.471
Situation, and Greeting, and Reply.

9
00:00:26.751 --> 00:00:28.543
Morning (until 12 pm).

10
00:00:28.823 --> 00:00:29.633
Greeting:

11
00:00:29.913 --> 00:00:30.831
Good morning!

12
00:00:31.111 --> 00:00:31.964
Reply:

13
00:00:32.244 --> 00:00:33.161
Good morning!

14
00:00:33.441 --> 00:00:34.380
How are you?

15
00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.772
Afternoon (12 to 5 pm).

16
00:00:37.052 --> 00:00:37.863
Greeting:

17
00:00:38.143 --> 00:00:39.231
Good afternoon!

18
00:00:39.511 --> 00:00:40.364
Reply:

19
00:00:40.644 --> 00:00:41.732
Good afternoon!

20
00:00:42.012 --> 00:00:43.804
Evening (after 5 pm).

21
00:00:44.084 --> 00:00:44.895
Greeting:

22
00:00:45.175 --> 00:00:46.049
Good evening!

23
00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:47.183
Reply:

24
00:00:47.463 --> 00:00:48.337
Good evening!

25
00:00:48.617 --> 00:00:49.961
Friendly, any time.

26
00:00:50.241 --> 00:00:51.052
Greeting:

27
00:00:51.332 --> 00:00:53.145
Hi! / Hello! / Hey!

28
00:00:53.425 --> 00:00:54.513
(friends only).

29
00:00:54.793 --> 00:00:55.647
Reply:

30
00:00:55.927 --> 00:00:56.609
Hi!

31
00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:57.913
How's it going?

32
00:00:58.193 --> 00:00:59.175
First meeting.

33
00:00:59.455 --> 00:01:00.265
Greeting:

34
00:01:00.545 --> 00:01:01.676
Nice to meet you.

35
00:01:01.956 --> 00:01:02.809
Reply:

36
00:01:03.089 --> 00:01:04.391
Nice to meet you too.

37
00:01:04.671 --> 00:01:05.481
Leaving.

38
00:01:05.761 --> 00:01:06.572
Greeting:

39
00:01:06.852 --> 00:01:09.711
Bye! / See you tomorrow! / Have a good day!

40
00:01:09.991 --> 00:01:10.844
Reply:

41
00:01:11.124 --> 00:01:12.511
You too! / Bye!

42
00:01:12.791 --> 00:01:13.687
Take care.

43
00:01:15.037 --> 00:01:18.365
Warning: \Good night\ is only for leaving.

44
00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:21.290
Good night means goodbye at night, or before sleep.

45
00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:23.959
When you arrive in the evening, say Good evening.

46
00:01:25.309 --> 00:01:26.184
Part 2.

47
00:01:26.464 --> 00:01:28.213
How are you? and good answers.

48
00:01:29.463 --> 00:01:30.807
Here is a quick table:

49
00:01:31.087 --> 00:01:32.922
Question, and Natural answers.

50
00:01:33.202 --> 00:01:34.162
How are you?:

51
00:01:34.442 --> 00:01:35.509
I'm good, thanks.

52
00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:37.794
And you? / Not bad, thank you.

53
00:01:38.074 --> 00:01:39.119
How about you?

54
00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:40.423
How's it going?:

55
00:01:40.703 --> 00:01:42.794
Pretty good! / Going well, thanks.

56
00:01:43.074 --> 00:01:44.311
How was your weekend?:

57
00:01:44.591 --> 00:01:45.871
It was great, thanks.

58
00:01:46.151 --> 00:01:47.538
I visited my parents.

59
00:01:47.818 --> 00:01:48.650
What's up?

60
00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:49.805
(casual):

61
00:01:50.085 --> 00:01:51.919
Not much! / Just working.

62
00:01:52.199 --> 00:01:52.839
You?

63
00:01:54.189 --> 00:01:55.384
Always ask back:

64
00:01:55.664 --> 00:01:57.285
And you? or How about you?

65
00:01:57.565 --> 00:01:59.379
It keeps the conversation going.

66
00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:01.625
Part 3.

67
00:02:01.905 --> 00:02:04.401
Introduce yourself: the 4-line formula.

68
00:02:05.651 --> 00:02:06.589
You could say:

69
00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:08.021
Hi, I'm Ashish.

70
00:02:08.301 --> 00:02:10.691
I'm a software developer at a product company.

71
00:02:10.971 --> 00:02:13.787
I'm from Lucknow, but I live in Bengaluru now.

72
00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:17.053
In my free time, I like cooking and watching cricket.

73
00:02:18.403 --> 00:02:19.747
Here is a quick table:

74
00:02:20.027 --> 00:02:21.691
Part, and Sentence starters.

75
00:02:21.971 --> 00:02:22.697
Name:

76
00:02:22.977 --> 00:02:25.793
I'm... / My name is... / You can call me...

77
00:02:26.073 --> 00:02:26.777
Work:

78
00:02:27.057 --> 00:02:31.430
I work as a... / I work at... / I'm a... / I'm studying...

79
00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:32.478
Place:

80
00:02:32.758 --> 00:02:38.113
I'm from... / I grew up in... / I live in... / I've lived in... for 5 years.

81
00:02:38.393 --> 00:02:39.246
Personal:

82
00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:44.497
I like... / I enjoy... / In my free time, I... / I'm interested in...

83
00:02:45.847 --> 00:02:46.764
Part 4.

84
00:02:47.044 --> 00:02:48.793
First questions to ask someone.

85
00:02:50.043 --> 00:02:52.902
What's your name? / Sorry, what was your name again?

86
00:02:53.182 --> 00:02:54.185
Where are you from?

87
00:02:54.465 --> 00:02:55.467
What do you do?

88
00:02:55.747 --> 00:02:57.283
(= What is your job?).

89
00:02:57.563 --> 00:02:59.867
How long have you been here or in this company?

90
00:03:00.147 --> 00:03:01.321
Do you live nearby?

91
00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:03.243
What do you like to do on weekends?

92
00:03:04.593 --> 00:03:05.553
Part 5.

93
00:03:05.833 --> 00:03:08.287
Conversation 1: meeting a new colleague.

94
00:03:09.537 --> 00:03:11.563
Here is how the conversation goes.

95
00:03:11.843 --> 00:03:12.633
Hi!

96
00:03:12.913 --> 00:03:14.342
I don't think we've met.

97
00:03:14.622 --> 00:03:15.646
I'm Priya.

98
00:03:15.926 --> 00:03:18.017
Hi Priya, nice to meet you.

99
00:03:18.297 --> 00:03:19.427
I'm Ashish.

100
00:03:19.707 --> 00:03:22.033
I joined the backend team on Monday.

101
00:03:22.313 --> 00:03:23.422
Oh, welcome!

102
00:03:23.702 --> 00:03:25.153
Nice to meet you too.

103
00:03:25.433 --> 00:03:26.905
Where were you before this?

104
00:03:27.185 --> 00:03:30.385
I was at a fintech company in Pune for six years.

105
00:03:30.665 --> 00:03:31.689
That's great.

106
00:03:31.969 --> 00:03:33.739
Are you from Pune originally?

107
00:03:35.089 --> 00:03:36.689
The conversation continues.

108
00:03:36.969 --> 00:03:38.463
No, I'm from Lucknow.

109
00:03:38.743 --> 00:03:41.623
But I've lived in Pune and now Bengaluru.

110
00:03:41.903 --> 00:03:43.183
How about you?

111
00:03:43.463 --> 00:03:44.785
I'm from Kochi.

112
00:03:45.065 --> 00:03:46.665
I've been here for three years.

113
00:03:46.945 --> 00:03:48.439
I'm on the mobile team.

114
00:03:48.719 --> 00:03:49.508
Nice!

115
00:03:49.788 --> 00:03:52.305
I'd love to learn how the mobile app works.

116
00:03:52.585 --> 00:03:54.633
Maybe we can have lunch sometime?

117
00:03:54.913 --> 00:03:56.577
Sure, let's do that this week.

118
00:03:57.927 --> 00:03:59.527
The conversation continues.

119
00:03:59.807 --> 00:04:00.554
Great.

120
00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:02.477
See you around, Priya!

121
00:04:03.827 --> 00:04:04.765
Part 6.

122
00:04:05.045 --> 00:04:07.264
Conversation 2: meeting a neighbour.

123
00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:10.541
Here is how the conversation goes.

124
00:04:10.821 --> 00:04:11.823
Hello!

125
00:04:12.103 --> 00:04:14.407
Are you the new family in 304?

126
00:04:14.687 --> 00:04:15.797
Yes, hello!

127
00:04:16.077 --> 00:04:17.954
We moved in last Saturday.

128
00:04:18.234 --> 00:04:19.365
I'm Ashish.

129
00:04:19.645 --> 00:04:20.733
Welcome!

130
00:04:21.013 --> 00:04:22.037
I'm Mr.

131
00:04:22.317 --> 00:04:24.173
Sharma, from 302.

132
00:04:24.453 --> 00:04:26.138
How are you finding the building?

133
00:04:26.418 --> 00:04:28.167
It's very nice, thank you.

134
00:04:28.447 --> 00:04:30.261
Everyone seems friendly.

135
00:04:30.541 --> 00:04:32.119
How long have you lived here?

136
00:04:33.469 --> 00:04:35.069
The conversation continues.

137
00:04:35.349 --> 00:04:36.800
Almost ten years now.

138
00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.979
If you need anything, just knock.

139
00:04:39.259 --> 00:04:40.752
That's very kind of you.

140
00:04:41.032 --> 00:04:42.291
Thank you, Mr.

141
00:04:42.571 --> 00:04:43.445
Sharma.

142
00:04:43.725 --> 00:04:44.984
Have a good evening!

143
00:04:45.264 --> 00:04:46.309
You too!

144
00:04:47.659 --> 00:04:48.598
Part 7.

145
00:04:48.878 --> 00:04:49.795
Practice.

146
00:04:51.045 --> 00:04:51.685
1.

147
00:04:51.965 --> 00:04:53.352
Choose the right greeting.

148
00:04:53.632 --> 00:04:54.784
It's 9 am.

149
00:04:55.064 --> 00:04:56.771
You meet your manager. then.

150
00:04:57.051 --> 00:04:58.203
It's 7 pm.

151
00:04:58.483 --> 00:05:00.296
You arrive at a party. then.

152
00:05:00.576 --> 00:05:01.685
It's 10 pm.

153
00:05:01.965 --> 00:05:03.821
You leave a friend's house. then.

154
00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:06.089
Success:

155
00:05:06.369 --> 00:05:07.222
Answers.

156
00:05:07.502 --> 00:05:08.419
Good morning!

157
00:05:08.699 --> 00:05:09.403
2.

158
00:05:09.683 --> 00:05:10.558
Good evening!

159
00:05:10.838 --> 00:05:11.585
3.

160
00:05:11.865 --> 00:05:12.718
Good night!

161
00:05:12.998 --> 00:05:14.619
(or Bye, have a good night!).

162
00:05:15.969 --> 00:05:16.673
2.

163
00:05:16.953 --> 00:05:22.159
Write your 4-line introduction using the formula above, then say it out loud 3 times.

164
00:05:22.439 --> 00:05:25.745
Time yourself: it should take about 20 to 30 seconds.

165
00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:26.772
3.

166
00:05:27.052 --> 00:05:28.183
Make the question.

167
00:05:28.463 --> 00:05:35.801
Write a question for each answer. ? then I'm from Jaipur. ? then I'm a data analyst. ? then I've been here for two years.

168
00:05:37.151 --> 00:05:38.069
Success:

169
00:05:38.349 --> 00:05:39.202
Answers.

170
00:05:39.482 --> 00:05:40.485
Where are you from?

171
00:05:40.765 --> 00:05:41.469
2.

172
00:05:41.749 --> 00:05:42.751
What do you do?

173
00:05:43.031 --> 00:05:43.778
3.

174
00:05:44.058 --> 00:05:45.445
How long have you been here?

175
00:05:46.795 --> 00:05:47.669
Part 8.

176
00:05:47.949 --> 00:05:48.995
Speak today.

177
00:05:50.245 --> 00:05:53.125
Greet 3 people with the right time-of-day greeting.

178
00:05:53.405 --> 00:05:57.778
Introduce yourself to one new person (or record your introduction on your phone).

179
00:05:58.058 --> 00:06:01.749
Ask someone How was your weekend? and ask one follow-up question.

180
00:06:03.099 --> 00:06:04.635
That's the end of this lesson.

181
00:06:04.915 --> 00:06:09.565
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

182
00:06:09.845 --> 00:06:15.968
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

